  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "The records collectively make the later result plausibly reconstructible. Multiple studies already use high-energy or mechanical alloying under argon followed by vacuum SPS to produce dense bulk, Ti-containing multicomponent HEAs, including systematic variation of milling time and examples of nanocrystalline feedstock. Earlier work also connects fine grains and solid solutions to grain-boundary and solid-solution strengthening, reports mixed BCC/FCC structures after SPS, and identifies Ti atomic size and melting-point-related behavior as important to phase formation and mechanical properties. Although the precise CoCrFeNiTi composition, short milling interval, 900–1000 °C SPS window, and exact 83/17 phase fraction are not disclosed together, an expert could plausibly combine the established processing route and strengthening principles to propose the later intervention and mechanism."
